   "name": "Thomas H. Kuchel Visitor Center",
   "parkCode": "redw",
   "description": "Southern-most visitor center in the park and located right on the beach. Exhibits about Yurok culture, art and history, redwood ecology, park information, junior ranger program, bookstore and retail sales. Park film available.",
   "latitude": "41.2868094650739",
   "longitude": "-124.09093463367094",
   "latLong": "{lat:41.2868094650739, lng:-124.09093463367094}",
   "audioDescription": "Located off HWY 101 in the southern part of the park. It is 1/4 mile to the west (ocean-side) of the HWY and there are signs showing where the turn off is. There is a 1/4-mile drive to a large parking area in front of the brown and grey facility, plenty of RV and trailer parking available. Information kiosks are in front of the steps and up to the entry doors. ADA accessible ramps is to the right and left side of the building. This facility is not visible from the road.",
